id: PropagateTagsAndPerformers
name: ᝯㄝₓ Propagate Tags and Performers to Related Entities
metadata:
  description: "Copies tags and performers from related entities onto the entity that links them.\n\nThirteen paths, each off until you enable it in the Path Settings dialog. Tags onto Scenes from their performers, studio, markers or groups; onto Galleries from their images; onto Images from their galleries; onto Groups from their scenes, studio, sub-groups, and from those scenes' performers and markers. Performers onto Scenes from their galleries, and onto Galleries from their images.\n\nCopy, never move - nothing is ever removed from the source.\n\nThree ways to run it: buttons on the target's Edit tab or the source's own detail page, automatically whenever Stash saves an entity, or as one library-wide task in Settings - Tasks - Plugin Tasks. The buttons and the automatic modes are off until you enable them below.\n\nNothing is written behind your back: a button either stages its additions in the edit form for you to save, or opens a dialog listing every change first - and so does the task. Nothing lands until you press Proceed, and Undo takes the run back while the dialog stays open.\n\nBACK UP YOUR DATABASE BEFORE THE FIRST RUN - it rewrites tag and performer assignments across the whole library and Stash has no undo.\n\nRequires Stash 0.31.0 or newer."
